{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK — `use_reactive` returns the passed reactive as-is, so the shared-state wiring is correct. So why was `params.value` `{}` in my harness test?\n\nAh wait — I see the issue in my test. In my `Harness`, I set `captured[\"params\"] = reactive_model_parameters` BEFORE calling `ModelController` and `ModelCreator`. Then `ModelCreator` sets `model_parameters.value = {...}` during render. But — `solara.render` may render the component, and the reactive value assignment (`model_parameters.value = ...`) triggers a re-render... The final read should still show the updated value.\n\nHmm, unless the reactive assignment happened and my read of `params.value` at line 40 ran BEFORE... no, it runs after render completes.\n\nWait — maybe the issue is different. Let me look again at my harness test output: \"2) reactive params initialized with defaults: {}\". \n\nHmm, hold on. Is it possible that `solara.render` in test mode renders without executing side effects... Let me debug directly: print params.value immediately, and also check whether ModelCreator's assignment line ran. Actually — wait. I bet the issue is this: in my harness, `ModelCreator` receives `{\"num_agents\": slider}` as `user_params`. Then `split_model_params` splits → `user_params` = `{\"num_agents\": Slider}` (Slider is not fixed). Then `model_parameters.value = {**fixed_params, **{k: v.get(\"value\") for k, v in user_params.items()}}` = `{\"num_agents\": 10}`. That should be set.\n\nUnless the exception occurred... no, no exception.\n\nHmm, wait — maybe `solara.use_reactive({})` in my Harness: the reactive is created fresh each render call with initial value `{}`... and on RE-render, `use_reactive` with a changing initial value updates the reactive to the new value! From the docstring: \"Note that that on each call, if the value changes, the reactive variable will be updated.\"\n\nSo the sequence in my harness render:\n1. `reactive_model_parameters = solara.use_reactive({})` → creates reactive with `{}`.\n2. `ModelController(...)`: calls `solara.use_reactive(reactive_model_parameters)` → returns same reactive.\n3. `ModelCreator(...)`: sets `model_parameters.value = {\"num_agents\": 10}`.\n4. Setting `.value` triggers re-render of Harness (reactive subscription? Actually use_reactive subscribes the component to value changes? Yes — \"The value changes trigger a re-render\").\n5. On re-render: `solara.use_reactive({})` is called AGAIN with initial `{}` — the value `{}` differs from current `{\"num_agents\": 10}`... wait no, use_reactive's initial-value-update behavior: \"If the argument passed changes the reactive variable will be updated.\" Hmm, that would reset it back to `{}`!\n\nHmm wait, but that would break SolaraViz too — it does `reactive_model_parameters = solara.use_reactive({})` at the top level, and ModelCreator mutates it → re-render → `use_reactive({})` called again... would reset to `{}`?!\n\nHmm, actually wait. Let me check whether `use_reactive` updates the value when the passed argument changes on re-render. Looking at the implementation would clarify. Let me read the rest of use_reactive.py.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"OK — `use_reactive` returns the passed reactive as-is, so the shared-state wiring is correct. So why was `params.value` `{}` in my harness test?\\n\\nAh wait — I see the issue in my test. In my `Harness`, I set `captured[\\\"params\\\"] = reactive_model_parameters` BEFORE calling `ModelController` and `ModelCreator`. Then `ModelCreator` sets `model_parameters.value = {...}` during render. But — `solara.render` may render the component, and the reactive value assignment (`model_parameters.value = ...`) triggers a re-render... The final read should still show the updated value.\\n\\nHmm, unless the reactive assignment happened and my read of `params.value` at line 40 ran BEFORE... no, it runs after render completes.\\n\\nWait — maybe the issue is different. Let me look again at my harness test output: \\\"2) reactive params initialized with defaults: {}\\\". \\n\\nHmm, hold on. Is it possible that `solara.render` in test mode renders without executing side effects... Let me debug directly: print params.value immediately, and also check whether ModelCreator's assignment line ran. Actually — wait. I bet the issue is this: in my harness, `ModelCreator` receives `{\\\"num_agents\\\": slider}` as `user_params`. Then `split_model_params` splits → `user_params` = `{\\\"num_agents\\\": Slider}` (Slider is not fixed). Then `model_parameters.value = {**fixed_params, **{k: v.get(\\\"value\\\") for k, v in user_params.items()}}` = `{\\\"num_agents\\\": 10}`. That should be set.\\n\\nUnless the exception occurred... no, no exception.\\n\\nHmm, wait — maybe `solara.use_reactive({})` in my Harness: the reactive is created fresh each render call with initial value `{}`... and on RE-render, `use_reactive` with a changing initial value updates the reactive to the new value! From the docstring: \\\"Note that that on each call, if the value changes, the reactive variable will be updated.\\\"\\n\\nSo the sequence in my harness render:\\n1. `reactive_model_parameters = solara.use_reactive({})` → creates reactive with `{}`.\\n2. `ModelController(...)`: calls `solara.use_reactive(reactive_model_parameters)` → returns same reactive.\\n3. `ModelCreator(...)`: sets `model_parameters.value = {\\\"num_agents\\\": 10}`.\\n4. Setting `.value` triggers re-render of Harness (reactive subscription? Actually use_reactive subscribes the component to value changes? Yes — \\\"The value changes trigger a re-render\\\").\\n5. On re-render: `solara.use_reactive({})` is called AGAIN with initial `{}` — the value `{}` differs from current `{\\\"num_agents\\\": 10}`... wait no, use_reactive's initial-value-update behavior: \\\"If the argument passed changes the reactive variable will be updated.\\\" Hmm, that would reset it back to `{}`!\\n\\nHmm wait, but that would break SolaraViz too — it does `reactive_model_parameters = solara.use_reactive({})` at the top level, and ModelCreator mutates it → re-render → `use_reactive({})` called again... would reset to `{}`?!\\n\\nHmm, actually wait. Let me check whether `use_reactive` updates the value when the passed argument changes on re-render. Looking at the implementation would clarify. Let me read the rest of use_reactive.py.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The shared-wiring is fine per the docs, but I need to check the \"value changes on re-render\" behavior that may reset state:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ff7df738898749d588e777a6","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n 80,140p /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/solara/hooks/use_reactive.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1017,"output":788,"cacheRead":29120,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":723,"totalTokens":30925,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788464494642,"responseId":"gen-1788464494-0XTCgzsGUKULuJH44KX5","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
