son.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Still `{}` after render. So `ModelCreator`'s body assignment `model_parameters.value = {...}` isn't persisting. Why?\\n\\nWait — the earlier trace showed the child component never rendered at all. Now ModelCreator is called directly inside the root harness. Did its body run? The assertion reads `state[\\\"params\\\"].value` == `{}`. \\n\\nHmm — is it possible the whole issue is: `solara.render` executes the root component, and `ModelCreator(model, user_params, ...)` — ModelCreator IS a solara component, so calling it creates a child element. Reacton renders child elements... The earlier trace showed the child never executed. Why would reacton not execute child components?\\n\\nOH WAIT. I bet I know what's happening! The first render of `Harness` raises an exception INSIDE... no.\\n\\nHmm, let me look at the earlier trace again: \\\"parent render: {}\\\" was the ONLY event. Child never rendered. And here ModelCreator's body seems not to have run (params still {}).\\n\\nActually — maybe the issue is different: maybe ModelCreator DID run and set the value, which triggered a re-render of the harness (since `use_reactive` value read → dependency), and on re-render... `solara.use_reactive({})` in CreatorHarness — wait, could `use_memo(update, [value])` re-run on render 2 because the dependency comparison uses `equals`... `update()` sets `reactive_value.value = value` ONLY if `not isinstance(value, Reactive)` — value here is the literal `{}` dict, so YES — if the memo re-runs, it would RESET the reactive to `{}`!!\\n\\nDoes `use_memo` re-run when deps are `{}` and previous `{}`? Memoization compares with equality. If solara's use_memo compares dependencies with `==`... `{}` == `{}` → True → no rerun. But if it compares with `is` or by id... `{}` is a NEW dict object each render → if comparison is identity-based, memo re-runs → value reset to `{}`!!\\n\\nLet me check solara's use_memo dependency comparison.