the main render tree.\n\nRather than fight this, the cleanest verification is:\n1. The unit-level `_check_model_params` tests (done, passing).\n2. The hook-warning removal (verified — no conditional warnings on full SolaraViz render).\n3. The reactive-params wiring: test `ModelCreator` directly as a top-level rendered component (like the existing tests do with `UserInputs`), verifying that `model_parameters` gets initialized with defaults and updates on slider change, and that reset-style re-instantiation works.\n\nLet me render `ModelCreator` directly as the root component (that's a fair test since `SolaraViz` just composes it), with a real reactive model + shared reactive params.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The existing tests only exercise the main-tree rendering. The sidebar with the sliders is rendered via solara's `Sidebar` context — in solara's app context, sidebar children are collected and rendered elsewhere. In test mode with `solara.render`, the `solara.Sidebar()` context captures its children into a separate widget (the `solara.Sidebar` component stores children in a side channel), so they're not in the main render tree.\\n\\nRather than fight this, the cleanest verification is:\\n1. The unit-level `_check_model_params` tests (done, passing).\\n2. The hook-warning removal (verified — no conditional warnings on full SolaraViz render).\\n3. The reactive-params wiring: test `ModelCreator` directly as a top-level rendered component (like the existing tests do with `UserInputs`), verifying that `model_parameters` gets initialized with defaults and updates on slider change, and that reset-style re-instantiation works.\\n\\nLet me render `ModelCreator` directly as the root component (that's a fair test since `SolaraViz` just composes it), with a real reactive model + shared reactive params.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Existing tests only exercise the main tree. Let me test the `ModelCreator`/`ModelController` composition directly as root components (that's where the fixed code lives):"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_224fc2a919494bceb068021b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /testbed && python - <<'EOF'\nimport warnings\nimport solara, mesa, ipyvuetify as vw\nfrom mesa.visualization.solara_viz import ModelCreator, ModelController, Slider, _check_model_params\n\nclass KwargsModel(mesa.Model):\n    def __init__(self, num_agents=10, **kwargs):\n        super().__init__(seed=None)\n        self.num_agents = num_agents\n        self.running = True\n    def step(self):\n        self.steps += 1\n\nslider = Slider(\"agents\", 10, 1, 50, 1)\nstate = {}\n\n@solara.component\ndef CreatorHarness(initial_model, user_params):\n    model = solara.use_reactive(initial_model)          # what SolaraViz does\n    model_parameters = solara.use_reactive({})          # shared reactive params\n    state[\"params\"] = model_parameters\n    state[\"model\"] = model\n    ModelController(model, model_parameters=model_parameters)\n    ModelCreator(model, user_params, model_parameters=model_parameters)\n    return solara.Text(\"ok\")\n\nwith warnings.catch_warnings(record=True) as w:\n    warnings.simplefilter(\"always\")\n    _, rc = solara.render(CreatorHarness(KwargsModel(), {\"num_agents\": slider}), handle_error=False)\nhook_w = [x for x in w if \"conditional\" in str(x.message) or \"use_reactive\" in str(x.message)]\nprint(\"1) hook warnings:\", hook_w or \"NONE ✓\")\n\nparams, model = state[\"params\"], state[\"model\"]\nprint(\"2) reactive params initialized:\", params.value)\nassert params.value == {\"num_agents\": 10}, params.value\nprint(\"   -> ModelCreator populated defaults into shared reactive ✓\")\n\n# user moves the slider -> on_change -> reinstantiate + update reactive\nrc.find(vw.Slider).widget.v_model = 25\nprint(\"3) after slider change -> params:\", params.value, \"| model.num_agents:\", model.value.num_agents)\nassert params.value == {\"num_agents\": 25}\nassert model.value.num_agents == 25\nprint(\"   -> on_change re-instantiated model with new param ✓\")\n\n# do_reset path (same code as ModelController.do_reset)\nmodel.value = model.value.__class__(**params.value)\nassert model.value.num_agents == 25\nprint(\"4) reset via model_parameters.value works ✓\")\n\n# step path\nmodel.value.step()\nprint(\"5) model.step() works, steps =\", model.value.steps, \"✓\")\n\n# _check_model_params matrix\n_check_model_params(KwargsModel.__init__, {\"anything\": 1, \"other\": 2})\n_check_model_params(KwargsModel.__init__, {})\nprint(\"6) kwargs model: no false missing/invalid errors ✓\")\n\nclass RequiredModel(mesa.Model):\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2): ...\nimport pytest\nwith pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Missing required model parameter: p2\"):\n    _check_model_params(RequiredModel.__init__, {\"p1\": 1})\nwith pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Invalid model parameter: bogus\"):\n    _check_model_params(RequiredModel.__init__, {\"p1\": 1, \"p2\": 2, \"bogus\": 3})\nprint(\"7) non-kwargs model: genuine errors still raised ✓\")\n\nclass MixedModel(mesa.Model):\n    def __init__(self, p1, **kwargs): ...\n_check_model_params(MixedModel.__init__, {\"p1\": 1, \"extra\": 5})\nprint(\"8) mixed model (required + **kwargs): extras allowed ✓\")\nprint(\"\\nALL CHECKS PASSED\")\nEOF"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":185,"output":1042,"cacheRead":35136,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":236,"totalTokens":36363,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788464619342,"responseId":"gen-1788464619-JuC20vrf5mT0r3qGuEMz","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_224fc2a919494bceb068021b","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/solara/core.py:33: UserWarning: Failed to validate hooks for component CreatorHarness: could not get source c