nder might not have exercised ModelController/ModelCreator at all in test mode! Let me verify the hook-warning removal more directly: render `ModelCreator` and `ModelController` components DIRECTLY (as roots, so they execute) and confirm no conditional warnings. The use_task event-loop issue blocks ModelController in sync mode... but the hook validation warning is emitted at component call time (solara/core.py:33 during element creation — `validate_hooks.HookValidator(obj).run()` runs when the component function is CALLED/element created), BEFORE any rendering. So I can simply CREATE the elements to trigger validation!\n\nLet me check solara/core.py around line 29-33.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The Sidebar uses `sidebar_portal.use_portal_add` — portal-based. In test renders, portal targets likely don't exist, so sidebar children render into a hidden div... Earlier full SolaraViz render had two hidden `Html` divs (`style_='display; none'`) at top — those might BE the portal/sidebar content containers! But their children showed as empty in the structure dump... Actually the earlier dump showed:\\n\\n```\\nchildren = [Html(... display none ...), Html(... display none ...), GridLayout(...)]\\n```\\n\\nThe hidden divs had no children listed. Hmm, but the sliders weren't found anywhere.\\n\\nOK — stepping back. The purpose of my end-to-end exercise was:\\n1. ✅ No conditional-hook warnings on SolaraViz render (verified — full SolaraViz render shows NONE; the AST validator checks all rendered components including ModelController/ModelCreator... wait, did ModelController/ModelCreator bodies actually RUN in the full render? The sidebar renders via portal — if the portal target doesn't exist in test mode, the sidebar children may never render!).\\n\\nHmm — so my \\\"no hook warnings\\\" verification on full SolaraViz render might not have exercised ModelController/ModelCreator at all in test mode! Let me verify the hook-warning removal more directly: render `ModelCreator` and `ModelController` components DIRECTLY (as roots, so they execute) and confirm no conditional warnings. The use_task event-loop issue blocks ModelController in sync mode... but the hook validation warning is emitted at component call time (solara/core.py:33 during element creation — `validate_hooks.HookValidator(obj).run()` runs when the component function is CALLED/element created), BEFORE any rendering. So I can simply CREATE the elements to trigger validation!\\n\\nLet me check solara/core.py around line 29-33.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The sidebar is portal-based (may not render in test mode). The hook validation runs at element creation time though — let me verify that directly:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_fe51546d16cf457781273a5e","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n 20,40p /usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/solara/core.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":682,"output":439,"cacheRead":48512,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":377,"totalTokens":49633,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788464955337,"responseId":"gen-1788464955-H2f820X8DYxNY2qoG3OE","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_fe51546d16cf457781273a5e","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"@overload\ndef component(obj: Callable[P, None], mime_bundle: Dict[str, Any] = ...) -> Callable[P, reacton.core.Element]: ...\n\n\ndef component(\n    obj: Union[Callable[P, None], FuncT, None] = None, mime_bundle: Dict[str, Any] = reacton.core.mime_bundle_default\n) -> Union[Callable[[FuncT], FuncT], FuncT, Callable[P, reacton.core.Element]]:\n    def wrapper(obj: Union[Callable[P, None], FuncT]) -> FuncT:\n        try:\n            validate_hooks.HookValidator(obj).run()\n        except Exception as e:\n            if not isinstance(e, validate_hooks.HookValidationError):\n                # we probably failed because of an unknown reason, but we do not want to break the user's code\n                warnings.warn(f\"Failed to validate hooks for component {obj.__qualname__}: {e}\")\n            else:\n                raise\n\n        return reacton.component(obj, mime_bundle)  # type: ignore\n\n    if obj is not None:\n        return wrapper(obj)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788464971978},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Important discovery: `solara.component`'s wrapper runs `HookValidator` at DECORATION time (module import), not at element creation. With `check_hooks == \"warn\"` (default), a HookValidationError is converted to... wait:\n\n```python\nexcept Exception as e:\n    if not isinstance(e, validate_hooks.HookValidationError):\n        warnings.warn(...)\n    else:\n        raise\n```\n\nHmm — if it IS a HookValidationError, it RAISES at decoration time?! But wait — in `HookValidator.run()`:\n\n```python\nexcept HookValidationError as e:\n    if solara.settings.main.check_hooks == \"error\":\n        raise e\n    elif solara.settings.main.check_hooks == \"warn\":\n        warnings.warn(str(e))\n```\n\nSo `run()` only re-raises when check_hooks == \"error\"; with \"warn\" it warns and returns normally. So at decoration time (import), the conditional-hook issue becomes a UserWarning. That's exactly what I reproduced at the very beginning:\n\n```\nUserWarning: /testbed/mesa/visualization/solara_viz.py:194: ModelController: `use_reactive` found within a conditional created on line 193\n```\n\nIt appeared when importing/using mesa.visualization.solara_viz — at decoration time. So the warning fires ONCE per process at import (when the decorator runs), regardless of rendering!\n\nMy verification: after the fix, re-importing mesa.visualization.solara_viz in a fresh process emits NO such warnings. The earlier full-SolaraViz renders after the fix showed no hook warnings — consistent.\n\nAlso note the AST validator checks the component source statically, so it flags the conditional pattern regardless of runtime behavior — my fix removes the pattern entirely from both components.\n\nLet me run the definitive verification in a fresh process: import mesa.visualization.solara_viz with warnings captured → expect zero hook warnings. Also re-run the ModelCreator-based end-to-end test (without ModelController to avoid the sync use_task limitation), and test the controller's reset/step logic directly (non-rendered).","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Important discovery: `solara.component`'s wrapper runs `HookValidator` at DECORATION time (module import), not at element creation. With `check_hooks == \\\"warn\\\"` (default), a HookValidationError is converted to... wait:\\n\\n```python\\nexcept Exception as e:\\n    if not isinstance(e, validate_hooks.HookValidationError):\\n        warnings.warn(...)\\n    else:\\n        raise\\n```\\n\\nHmm — if it IS a HookValidationError, it RAISES at decoration time?! But wait — in `HookValidator.run()`:\\n\\n```python\\nexcept HookValidationError as e:\\n    if solara.settings.main.check_hooks == \\\"error\\\":\\n        raise e\\n    elif solara.settings.main.check_hooks == \\\"warn\\\":\\n        warnings.warn(str(e))\\n```\\n\\nSo `run()` only re-raises when check_hooks == \\\"error\\\"; with \\\"warn\\\" it warns and returns normally. So at decoration time (import), the conditional-hook issue becomes a UserWarning. That's exactly what I reproduced at the very beginning:\\n\\n```\\nUserWarning: /testbed/mesa/visualization/solara_viz.py:194: ModelController: `use_reactive` found within a conditional created on line 193\\n```\\n\\nIt appeared when importing/using mesa.visualization.solara_viz — at decoration time. So the warning fires ONCE per process at import (when the decorator runs), regardless of rendering!\\n\\nMy verification: after the fix, re-importing mesa.visualization.solara_viz in a fresh process emits NO such warnings. The earlier full-SolaraViz renders after the fix showed no hook warnings — consistent.\\n\\nAlso note the AST validator checks the component source statically, so it flags the conditional pattern regardless of runtime behavior — my fix removes the pattern entirely from both components.\\n\\nLet me run the definitive verification in a fresh process: import mesa.visualization.solara_viz with warnings captured → expect zero hook warnings. Also re-run the ModelCreator-based end-to-end test (without ModelController to avoid the sync use_task limitation), and test the controller's reset/step logic directly (non-rendered).\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"Key insight: hook validation runs at decoration time (import), so the definitive check is importing the module in a fresh process. Let me run the complete verification suite:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9f4e5a5cc6be4bbdb3d571b2","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /testbed && python - <<'EOF'\nimport warnings\n\n# ===== 1. Definitive hook-warning check: fresh import of the module =====\nwith warnings.catch_warnings(record=True) as w:\n    warnings.simplefilter(\"always\")\n    import mesa.visualization.solara_viz  # decorators run HookValidator here\nhook_w = [x for x in w if \"conditional\" in str(x.message) or \"use_reactive\" in str(x.message)\n          or \"SH102\" in str(x.message) or \"rules of hooks\" in str(x.message)]\nprint(\"1) import-time hook warnings:\", hook_w or \"NONE ✓\")\nassert not hook_w\n\nimport solara, mesa, ipyvuetify as vw, pytest\nfrom mesa.visualization.solara_viz import ModelCreator, Slider, _check_model_params\n\nclass KwargsModel(mesa.Model):\n    def __init__(self, num_agents=10, **kwargs):\n        super().__init__(seed=None)\n        self.num_agents = num_agents\n        self.running = True\n    def step(self):\n        self.steps += 1\n\nslider = Slider(\"agents\", 10, 1, 50, 1)\nstate = {}\n\n@solara.component\ndef Harness(initial_model, user_params):\n    model = solara.use_reactive(initial_model)\n    model_parameters = solara.use_reactive({})   # shared reactive params (SolaraViz pattern)\n    state[\"params\"] = model_parameters\n    state[\"model\"] = model\n    creator = ModelCreator(model, user_params, model_parameters=model_parameters)\n    return creator   # include element so it actually renders\n\n# ===== 2. Render WITHOUT ModelController (avoids sync use_task limitation) =====\nwith warnings.catch_warnings(record=True) as w:\n    warnings.simplefilter(\"always\")\n    _, rc = solara.render(Harness(KwargsModel(), {\"num_agents\": slider}), handle_error=False)\nhook_w = [x for x in w if \"conditional\" in str(x.message) or \"use_reactive\" in str(x.message)]\nprint(\"2) ModelCreator render hook warnings:\", hook_w or \"NONE ✓\")\nassert not hook_w\n\nparams, model = state[\"params\"], state[\"model\"]\nprint(\"3) reactive params initialized from defaults:\", params.value)\nassert params.value == {\"num_agents\": 10}\nprint(\"   -> parameter tracking initialized correctly (no initial params given) ✓\")\n\n# ===== 3. User changes slider -> on_change path =====\nrc.find(vw.Slider).widget.v_model = 25\nprint(\"4) after slider change -> params:\", params.value, \"| new model num_agents:\", model.value.num_agents)\nassert params.value == {\"num_agents\": 25} and model.value.num_agents == 25\nprint(\"   -> reactive state management consistent ✓\")\n\n# ===== 4. Reset path (ModelController.do_reset logic) =====\nmodel.value = model.value.__class__(**params.value)\nassert model.value.num_agents == 25\nmodel.value.step()\nassert model.value.steps == 1\nprint(\"5) reset via model_parameters.value + stepping works ✓\")\n\n# ===== 5. Render WITH initial params provided (KwargsModel(num_agents=7)) =====\nstate.clear()\n_, rc2 = solara.render(Harness(KwargsModel(num_agents=7), {\"num_agents\": slider}), handle_error=False)\nassert state[\"params\"].value == {\"num_agents\": 10}\nprint(\"6) render with initial model params: works ✓\")\n\n# ===== 6. _check_model_params behavior matrix =====\n_check_model_params(KwargsModel.__init__, {\"anything\": 1, \"other\": 2})   # extras OK\n_check_model_params(KwargsModel.__init__, {})                            # nothing required\nprint(\"7) kwargs model: no false missing/invalid errors ✓\")\n\nclass RequiredModel(mesa.Model):\n    def __init__(self, p1, p2): ...\nwith pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Missing required model parameter: p2\"):\n    _check_model_params(RequiredModel.__init__, {\"p1\": 1})\nwith pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Invalid model parameter: bogus\"):\n    _check_model_params(RequiredModel.__init__, {\"p1\": 1, \"p2\": 2, \"bogus\": 3})\nprint(\"8) non-kwargs model: genuine errors still raised ✓\")\n\nclass MixedModel(mesa.Model):\n    def __init__(self, p1, **kwargs): ...\n_check_model_params(MixedModel.__init__, {\"p1\": 1, \"extra\": 5})  # required met, extras OK\nwith pytest.raises(ValueError, match=\"Missing required model parameter: p1\"):\n    _check_model_params(MixedModel.__init__, {})\nprint(\"9) mixed model (required + **kwargs): required enforced, extras allowed ✓\")\n\nprint(\"\\n*** ALL CHECKS PASSED ***\")\nEOF"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":1035,"output":1489,"cacheRead":48832,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":427,"totalTokens":51356,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788464971983,"responseId":"gen-1788464972-n5RP1nytxOEO8Rizduy5","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_9f4e5a5cc6be4bbdb3d571b2","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/usr/local/lib/python3.11/site-packages/solara/core.py:33: UserWarning: Failed to validate hooks for component Harness: could not get source code\n  warnings.warn(f\"Failed to validate hooks for component {obj.__qualname__}: {e}\")\n1