alue = {'num_agents': 25}`.\n\nThen why does `params.value` read 10?\n\nOH WAIT. I see it — in my Harness:\n\n```python\nmodel = solara.use_reactive(initial_model)\n```\n\n`use_reactive(initial_model)` — when Harness RE-RENDERS (triggered by model.value change or params change), `use_memo(update, [value])` in use_reactive: `value` is `initial_model` — a NEW KwargsModel instance? No — `initial_model` is the same object passed at element creation... elements don't re-create on re-render; Harness's body re-executes with the SAME args (`initial_model` is the same object). Deep equality → memo hit → no update. OK.\n\nHmm, so why is params.value stale? Let me think about `model_parameters.value = new_model_parameters` — assigning a reactive's value inside a change handler (not during render)... \n\nOH WAIT. I know! `state[\"params\"] = model_parameters` — captured during render 1. But on CHANGE, `on_change` runs INSIDE ModelCreator's closure where `model_parameters` is the local from the render in which `UserInputs` was rendered. Same object though...\n\nHmm, unless use_reactive created a NEW reactive on re-render! Look:\n\n```python\nreactive_value = solara.use_memo(create, dependencies=[])\nif isinstance(value, solara.Reactive):\n    reactive_value = value\n```\n\n`use_memo(create, [])` — `create()` returns `None` when value is Reactive (no store created). Memo hit on re-render → None → `reactive_value = value` → same. Fine.\n\nHmm, what about `solara.use_reactive({})` in MY Harness — the `{}` literal: `use_memo(update, [value])` with value={}. On re-render: deep-equals → memo hit → `update()` NOT called → no reset. Fine.\n\nSo why stale?! Let me debug: print `id(state[\"params\"])`, check whether on_change's assignment happened at all, and whether there are multiple reactive objects. Maybe the issue: `rc.find(vw.Slider).widget.v_model = 25` — setting v_model triggers solara's slider `on_value` → `change_handler(value)` with `name` bound... then `on_change(name, value)`